# OPUS-NODATA-20260929-03 (plan §7b "Повторный вход без data-двойника", "Сохранить правильную адресацию при удалении
# lmx_fresh"; L2 §18.2): `@x` of a declared field is the address of its typed cell in M's occurrence -- one cell for
# every activation of M, the outer and a re-entrant one; no per-call instance, no address of a working copy.  The
# outer takes p: @x and calls M again; the re-entrant activation takes its own @x and writes 55 through it; the outer
# reads \p: 55 -- the same cell.  A per-call instance, or `@x` lowered to the working value's address (the old C-cache
# lowering the author rejected), reads the outer's own 0.  Native only: the walk takes no address (the walked single
# place: unit_walk_cache_reentry_peek).  Success 7; 0 is 65.
fn: M (int: n) int
    int: x 0
    @: int p
    p: @x
    if: n > 0
        M(n - 1)
        int: seen 0
        seen: \p
        return: seen
    @: int q
    q: @x
    \q: 55
    return: 0
end: M
int: r 0
r: M(1)
int: ok 64
if: r = 55
    ok: 7
if: r = 0
    ok: 65
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
